# Kompis Core — Authenticated Customer Workspace

Task: `AIPIFY.KOMPIS.CORE.AUTHENTICATED.CUSTOMER.WORKSPACE.V1`

## Clean Core only

- No customer names, pilot names, customer domains, or customer-specific routes/modules/types in Core.
- Use generic terms: customer, tenant, workspace, member area, module, entity, role, access tier, tool, action.
- Reference fixtures only: `reference_customer_*`, `reference_member_portal`, etc.

## Ownership

- Core owns `kompis_customer_workspace_contract` and permission evaluation.
- Customer explicitly activates public/authenticated access, tools, knowledge, and confirmation policies.
- Fail-closed by default — no implicit tool access, no auto-activation.

## Session & public runtime

- Public and authenticated sessions are separated; handoff requires server rebind.
- Anonymous claims never upgrade to authenticated claims.
- Verified public Website Kompis runtime remains protected — do not change ask/embed pipelines incompatibly.
- On logout, authenticated tools are removed immediately.

## Tools & security

- No direct database access from Kompis tools.
- No tool without contract allowlist.
- No write without confirmation policy; Kompis never confirms for the user.
- No more access than the current authenticated user.
- Private messages disabled by default.
- Audit permission changes, tool invocations, and confirmations.

## Locale

- Dynamic global locale list from Core language foundation.
- English fallback; never show raw keys; never hardcode locale unions in workspace UI.

## Branding & proof

- Customer branding via canonical theme contract only.
- Authenticated Production proof required before Production Ready.
